A1. Woolworth diamonds. ~ GLASS
A6. Something she doesn't have to try hard to do to you if she wants a kiss. ~ TEMPT
A10. To endeavor. ~ AIM
A11. Something you're sure to find every week in JUDGE. ~ LAUGH
A14. Something girls always give flat tires. ~ AIR
A15. Abbreviation for a word meaning highway. ~ ST
A16. If you buy something from a Hebrew and sell it at a profit to a Scotchman what would you call it? (Not miracle.) ~ BARGAIN
A18. A Greek letter. ~ NU
A19. A kind of a bean. ~ SOY
A20. An expensive part of fish. ~ ROE
A22. It's necessary to do this quite often if you want to live to be very old. ~ EAT
A24. English noblemen. ~ EARLS
A27. To procure. ~ GET
A29. A sign you see in front of a moving picture theater where JUDGE's crossword puzzles are being shown. ~ SRO
A30. A New England State (abr.). ~ RI
A31. A preposition of place. ~ AT
A32. Something you get a lot of without paying for at any place but a filling station. ~ GAS
A33. They don't come any greener than this. ~ GRASS
A35. You will get a lot of these if you advertise for a stenographer. ~ TYPES
A37. This is what makes it hot for people. ~ FUEL
A38. George Washington never told one of these. (That should be a hard one.) ~ LIE
A40. If you ever get one of these treat it kindly and then execute it. ~ IDEA
A42. That is (abr.). ~ IE
A43. How you should feel at Christmas (at least before the bills come in). ~ MERRY
A45. District famous for Congressmen (enough said) (abr.). ~ DC
A46. A period of time. ~ ERA
A48. East Baltic Oysters. (Try and get 'em!) (abr.). ~ EBO
A51. In a slanting position. ~ ASLANT
A54. A dangerous color. (Ask most any married man.) ~ BLONDE
A56. Feminine definite article (French). ~ LA
A57. Venician taxicab. ~ GONDOLA
A58. Where an aeroplane goes. ~ UP
A59. Something Valentino is at making love. ~ EXPERT
A60. Few husbands can do this themselves in their own homes. ~ ASSERT

D1. What a barber does when he cuts your hair. ~ GASSES
D2. The way most men occasionally come home. ~ LIT
D3. Part of the verb to be. ~ AM
D4. Killers. ~ SLAYERS
D5. A kind of a bowl that sugar is sometimes put in. ~ SUGAR
D6. Something you would probably be if you were in the middle of the Sahara desert, without food or drink and had lost your compass. ~ THIRSTY
D7. Girls have been known to call their mothers this. ~ MA
D8. If you see one of these, pick it up. ~ PIN
D9. Credits. ~ TRUSTS
D12. Arabia (abr.). ~ AR
D13. A State famous for peaches (abr.). ~ GA
D16. A knight of the road. (Slang.) ~ BO
D17. A feminine word that is terribly misused. ~ NO
D19. A place where you can buy bird seed and automobile goggles. ~ STORE
D21. Something ham actors often get. ~ EGGED
D23. It doesn't pay to do this with your wife. ~ ARGUE
D25. Something in a church that seems miles long to the groom. ~ AISLE
D26. When does a woman meet you when you have a date with her at seven o'clock? ~ LATER
D28. Relieved. ~ EASED
D34. Governor of New York. (You know me — ) ~ AL
D36. A Greek letter. ~ PI
D37. The last act in the follies. ~ FINALE
D39. Anger. ~ IRE
D41. Something most any girl will do when invited to ride in a Rolls Royce. ~ ACCEPT
D43. The district over which a lord of the Middle Ages held authority. ~ MANOR
D44. Something an active cheer leader does. ~ YELLS
D46. The (Spanish). ~ EL
D47. Something you shouldn't fly in. ~ RAGE
D49. Very large snakes. ~ BOAS
D50. Preposition. ~ ON
D52. An instrument of torture (abr.). ~ SAX
D53. Initials of a dangerous explosive. ~ TNT
D54. Something to be used around the neck (not soap). ~ BOA
D55. A French word meaning "hard." ~ DUR


